            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/InternalLogicInSlicesOfVect-230406.jpg", :width => "600"}/
          %p
            The historical debate
            %a{:href => "#History"} above
            about justifying BvN logic as a formal logic is ultimately rooted in the fact that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
            is not a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed category
            (much less a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+category"} locally cartesian closed category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            is exotic.
