          %h2#References Literature
          %h3#original_articles Original articles
          %p The original proposal on quantum logic:
          %ul
            %li#BirkhoffvonNeumann36
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Garrett+Birkhoff"}> Garrett Birkhoff
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+von+Neumann"} John von Neumann
              = succeed "," do
                %em The logic of quantum mechanics
              %strong 37
              823-843 (1936) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/1968621"}> doi:10.2307/1968621
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Historical account of
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+von+Neumann"} John von Neumann
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/von+Neumann+algebra+factors"} von Neumann algebra factors
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Miklos+R%C3%A9dei"}> Miklos Rédei
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Why John von Neumann did not Like the Hilbert Space formalism of quantum mechanics (and what he liked instead)
              %strong 27
              4 (1996) 493-510 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S1355-2198(96)00017-2"}> doi:10.1016/S1355-2198(96)00017-2
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karl+Svozil"}> Karl Svozil
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum Logic
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/9789814021074"} ISBN:9789814021074
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karl+Svozil"}> Karl Svozil
                \:
                %em Quantum logic. A brief outline
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/9902042"}> arXiv:quant-ph/9902042
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Proposal for an enhancement of the Birkhoff-von Neumann axioms by
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+measures"} probability measures
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+Mackey"}> George Mackey
              , Section 2-2 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Mathematical Foundations of Quantum Mechanics: a Lecture-note Volume
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://books.google.de/books?id=qlpb2mWYmfYC&printsec=frontcover&hl=de&source=gbs_ge_summary_r&cad=0#v=onepage&q&f=false"} google books
          %p further discussed in:
          %ul
            %li#Gleason57
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Gleason"}> Andrew Gleason
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Measures on the closed subspaces of a Hilbert space
                %strong 6
                4 (1957), 885-893 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.iumj.indiana.edu/IUMJ/FULLTEXT/1957/6/56050"}> IUMJ:56050
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.iumj.indiana.edu/IUMJ/FTDLOAD/1957/6/56050/pdf"} pdf
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gleason%27s+theorem"}> Gleason's theorem
                  )
            %li
              %p
                Samuel S. Holland Jr.,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Orthomodularity in infinite dimensions; a theorem of M. Solèr
                %strong 32
                (1995) 205-234 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9504224"}> arXiv:math.RA/9504224
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Pavlos Kazakopoulos, Georgios Regkas,
                %em Infinite Permutation Groups and the Origin of Quantum Mechanics
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.13044"}> arXiv:2307.13044
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            An account of quantum logic within a comprehensive discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
            and its
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interpretation+of+quantum+mechanics"} interpretation of quantum mechanics
          %ul
            %li#Scheibe73
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Erhard+Scheibe"}> Erhard Scheibe
              , pp 71 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em The logical analysis of quantum mechanics
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+logic"} categorical logic
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+categories"} symmetric monoidal categories
            (not just of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            but of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+logic"} linear logic
            as quantum logic:
          %ul
            %li#Crown75
              G. D. Crown,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On some orthomodular posets of vector bundles
              %strong 15
              1-2 (1975) 11-25
          %p much later followed up in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Harding"}> John Harding
              , Taewon Yang,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Logic of Bundles
              %strong 54
              12 (2015) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/s10773-015-2760-6"}> doi:10.1007/s10773-015-2760-6
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The introduction of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+logic"} linear logic
            with the suggestion of a possible relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+physics"} quantum physics
          %ul
            %li#Girard87
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Yves+Girard"}> Jean-Yves Girard
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Linear logic
              %strong 50
              1 (1987) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0304-3975(87)90045-4"}> doi:10.1016/0304-3975(87)90045-4
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p but remaining undecided:
          %blockquote
            %p#WildHopes
              %a{:href => "#Girard87"}> Girard (1987), p. 7
              \: “One of the wild hopes that this suggests is the possibility of a direct connection with quantum mechanics… but let’s not dream too much!”
          %p
            The relation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+logic"} linear logic
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantales"} quantales
          %ul
            %li#Yetter90
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Yetter"}> David Yetter
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantales and (noncommutative) linear logic
              %strong 55
              (1990) 41-64 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/2274953"}> doi:10.2307/2274953
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Maybe the first to really say that linear logic is a good kind of quantum logic:
          %ul
            %li#Pratt92
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vaughan+Pratt"}> Vaughan Pratt
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Linear logic for generalized quantum mechanics
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://www.computer.org/csdl/proceedings/phycmp/1992/12OmNx19jVS"} Workshop on Physics and Computation (PhysComp’92)
                (1992) 166-180 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.ieeecomputersociety.org/10.1109/PHYCMP.1992.615518"}> doi:10.1109/PHYCMP.1992.615518
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://boole.stanford.edu/pub/ql.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Pratt-LinearLogicForQuantum.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#Pratt93
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vaughan+Pratt"}> Vaughan Pratt
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The second calculus of binary relations
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 711
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-57182-5_9"} doi:10.1007/3-540-57182-5_9
              %blockquote
                %p
                  “Linear logic is seen in its best light as the realization of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Curry-Howard+isomorphism"} Curry-Howard isomorphism
                  for
                  = succeed "\u201D" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+algebra"} linear algebra
          %p
            First practical development of this perspective (see
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+information+theory+in+terms+of+dagger-compact+categories"}> quantum information theory in terms of dagger-compact categories
              ):
          %ul
            %li#AbramskyCoecke
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Samson+Abramsky"}> Samson Abramsky
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bob+Coecke"} Bob Coecke
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A categorical semantics of quantum protocols
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0402130"} arXiv:quant-ph/0402130
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1109/LICS.2004.1319636"} doi:10.1109/LICS.2004.1319636
            %li#AbramskyDuncan05
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Samson+Abramsky"}> Samson Abramsky
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Duncan"} Ross Duncan
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Categorical Quantum Logic
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0512114"} arXiv:quant-ph/0512114
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0960129506005275"} doi:10.1017/S0960129506005275
            %li#Duncan06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Duncan"}> Ross Duncan
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Types for quantum mechanics
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://personal.strath.ac.uk/ross.duncan/papers/rduncan-thesis.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.cs.ox.ac.uk/people/ross.duncan/talks/2005/pps-22-05-2005.pdf"} slides
          %p
            and as a paradigm for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+programming+languages"} quantum programming languages
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+lambda-calculus"}> quantum lambda-calculus
            ):
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beno%C3%AEt+Valiron"}> Benoît Valiron
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A functional programming language for quantum computation with classical control
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.20381/ruor-18372"} doi:10.20381/ruor-18372
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://ruor.uottawa.ca/bitstream/10393/26790/1/MR01625.PDF"} pdf
            %li#SelingerValiron04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Selinger"}> Peter Selinger
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beno%C3%AEt+Valiron"} Benoît Valiron
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A lambda calculus for quantum computation with classical control
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/cs/0404056"} arXiv:cs/0404056
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/11417170_26"} doi:10.1007/11417170_26
            %li#SelingerValiron09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Selinger"}> Peter Selinger
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beno%C3%AEt+Valiron"} Benoît Valiron
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum Lambda Calculus
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Semantic Techniques in Quantum Computation
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139193313.005"} doi:10.1017/CBO9781139193313.005
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.mscs.dal.ca/~selinger/papers/qlambdabook.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            That therefore in particular categories of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+spaces"} phase spaces
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+cobordisms"} categories of cobordisms
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domains"} domains
            of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FQFT"} functorial quantum field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+logic"} linear logic
            has been highlighted in
          %ul
            %li#Baez04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum Quandaries: a Category-Theoretic Perspective
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The structural foundations of quantum gravity
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0404040"} arXiv:quant-ph/0404040
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://global.oup.com/academic/product/the-structural-foundations-of-quantum-gravity-9780199269693"} ISBN:9780199269693
            %li#Slavnov05
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergey+Slavnov"}> Sergey Slavnov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em From proof-nets to bordisms: the geometric meaning of multiplicative connectives
                %strong 15
                06 (2005) 1151-1178 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0960129505004974"}> doi:10.1017/S0960129505004974
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergey+Slavnov"}> Sergey Slavnov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Geometrical semantics for linear logic (multiplicative fragment)
                %strong 357
                1-3 (2006) 215-229 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tcs.2006.03.020"}> doi:10.1016/j.tcs.2006.03.020
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            For more exposition along these lines see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BaezStay09"} Baez &amp; Stay (2009)
          %p
            Interpreting the
            = succeed "-sector" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+logic"} linear logic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bunched+logic"} bunched logic
            as a quantum logic:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Li+Zhou"}> Li Zhou
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gilles+Barthe"} Gilles Barthe
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Justin+Hsu"} Justin Hsu
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mingsheng+Ying"} Mingsheng Ying
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nengkun+Yu"} Nengkun Yu
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Quantum Interpretation of Bunched Logic for Quantum Separation Logic
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2102.00329"} arXiv:2102.00329
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1109/LICS52264.2021.9470673"} doi:10.1109/LICS52264.2021.9470673
          %h3#review_and_exposition Review and Exposition
          %p Early general introductions and survey:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Itamar+Pitowsky"}> Itamar Pitowsky
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum Probability – Quantum Logic
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 321
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0021186"} doi:10.1007/BFb0021186
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (including discussion of
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+probability+theory"} quantum probability theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roland+Omn%C3%A8s"}> Roland Omnès
                , §5 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Interpretation+of+Quantum+Mechanics"} The Interpretation of Quantum Mechanics
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://press.princeton.edu/titles/5525.html"} ISBN:9780691036694
            %li
              %p
                Pavel Pták , Sylvia Pulmannová ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Orthomodular structures as quantum logics
                %strong 44
                Kluwer, Springer (1991) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/9780792312079"}> ISBN:978-0-7923-1207-9
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Kurt Engesser, Dov M. Gabbay, Daniel Lehmann (eds.)
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Quantum+Logic+and+Quantum+Structures"} Handbook of Quantum Logic and Quantum Structures
                Elsevier (2009) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.sciencedirect.com/book/9780444528698"}> ISBN:9780080931661
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p A bibliography of hundreds of works up to 1992:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mladen+Pavi%C4%8Di%C4%87"}> Mladen Pavičić
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Bibliography on quantum logics and related structures
              %strong 31
              (1992) 373–455 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00739999"}> doi:10.1007/BF00739999
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.irb.hr/users/mpavicic/papers-ps-pdf/quantum-logic/1992-int-j-theor-phys-1.pdf"} pdf
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Franco+Strocchi"}> Franco Strocchi
                , §2.5 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An introduction to the mathematical structure of quantum mechanics
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 28
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/7038"} doi:10.1142/7038
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quantum_logic"} Quantum logic
            %li
              %p
                Stanford encyclopaedia of philosophy,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://plato.stanford.edu/entries/qt-quantlog"} Quantum logic and probability theory
          %p
            Critique of Birkhoff-von Neumann logic in contrast to
            = succeed ":" do
